(1. Introduction) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 417.8899999999999864 Td
(The Periodic Labour Force Survey \(PLFS\) is India's flagship household survey for measuring labour market indicators.) Tj
T* (Launched by the National Statistical Office \(NSO\), MoSPI in April 2017, PLFS replaced the earlier quinquennial) Tj
T* (Employment-Unemployment Surveys \(EUS\) conducted by the erstwhile NSSO.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 370.8899999999999864 Td
(PLFS provides estimates of key labour force indicators on two time frequencies:) Tj
T* (- **Annual estimates**: For both rural and urban areas \(July-June reference period\)) Tj
T* (- **Quarterly estimates**: For urban areas only \(January-March, April-June, July-September, October-December\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 323.8899999999999864 Td
(This dual-frequency design enables timely monitoring of urban labour markets while maintaining comprehensive annual) Tj
T* (coverage of both rural and urban areas.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 277.8899999999999864 Td
(2. Survey Design) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 259.8899999999999864 Td
(2.1 Sample Design) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 244.8899999999999864 Td
(PLFS uses a stratified multi-stage design:) Tj
T* (- First Stage Units \(FSUs\): Census villages \(rural\) and Urban Frame Survey \(UFS\) blocks \(urban\)) Tj
T* (- Second Stage Units: Households) Tj
T* (- Stratification: Rural areas stratified by 4 MPCE classes; Urban areas stratified by town size class.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Sample size: ~1.02 lakh households per year \(about 7,200 FSUs, with urban FSUs revisited quarterly for the panel) Tj
T* (design\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 143.8899999999999864 Td
(2.2 Rotating Panel in Urban Areas) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 128.8899999999999864 Td
(Urban FSUs are divided into 4 sub-samples \(rotation groups\). Each sub-sample is surveyed in one quarter and then) Tj
T* (re-surveyed in the same quarter of the following year. This panel structure enables quarter-on-quarter and) Tj
T* (year-on-year comparison for urban labour market dynamics.) Tj
ET
