(2.3 Reference Period for Employment) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 753.8899999999999864 Td
(PLFS uses multiple reference periods:) Tj
T* (- **Usual Activity \(Principal + Subsidiary\)**: 365 days preceding the date of survey) Tj
T* (- **Current Weekly Status \(CWS\)**: 7 days preceding the date of survey) Tj
T* (- **Current Daily Status \(CDS\)**: Each day of the reference week \(7 days\)) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The choice of reference period affects measured employment and unemployment rates significantly.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 653.8899999999999864 Td
(3. Key Concepts and Definitions) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 635.8899999999999864 Td
(3.1 Labour Force) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 620.8899999999999864 Td
(The labour force comprises all persons who are either employed or unemployed \(seeking and available for work\)) Tj
T* (during the reference period. Labour Force = Employed + Unemployed.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 584.8899999999999864 Td
(3.2 Worker Population Ratio \(WPR\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 569.8899999999999864 Td
(WPR = \(Number of persons employed / Population\) × 100) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Also called Employment Rate. Measures the proportion of the population that is employed. A high WPR can reflect) Tj
T* (both genuine employment and necessity-driven employment \(e.g., distress employment in agriculture\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 507.8899999999999864 Td
(3.3 Labour Force Participation Rate \(LFPR\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 492.8899999999999864 Td
(LFPR = \(Labour Force / Population\) × 100) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Measures the proportion of the population that is either employed or actively seeking employment. Low LFPR) Tj
T* (among women and youth is a key structural feature of India's labour market.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 430.8899999999999864 Td
(3.4 Unemployment Rate \(UR\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 415.8899999999999864 Td
(UR = \(Unemployed / Labour Force\) × 100) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Measures the proportion of the labour force that is without work but seeking and available for work. India's) Tj
T* (unemployment rate is relatively low by international standards but disguised unemployment \(underemployment\) is) Tj
T* (significant.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 340.8899999999999864 Td
(3.5 Usual Principal Activity \(UPS\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 325.8899999999999864 Td
(The activity in which a person spent the major time during the 365 days preceding the survey date. Used for) Tj
T* (classifying persons into broad categories: workers, unemployed, and out-of-labour-force \(students, domestic duties,) Tj
T* (etc.\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 276.8899999999999864 Td
(3.6 Usual Subsidiary Activity \(USS\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 261.8899999999999864 Td
(Activity pursued for a minor part of the year in addition to the principal activity. Adding USS to UPS gives the "usual) Tj
T* (activity \(principal + subsidiary\)" or UPSS measure, which captures a broader segment of workers, particularly) Tj
T* (seasonal agricultural workers.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 212.8899999999999864 Td
(3.7 Current Weekly Status \(CWS\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 197.8899999999999864 Td
(Employment status determined based on activities during the 7 days preceding the survey date. A person is) Tj
T* (employed \(CWS\) if they worked for at least one hour on at least one day during the reference week.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 161.8899999999999864 Td
(3.8 Current Daily Status \(CDS\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 146.8899999999999864 Td
(Determined for each day of the reference week. A person can be employed for part of a day and unemployed for the) Tj
T* (rest. CDS measures person-days of work and unemployment. CDS unemployment rate is highest among the three) Tj
T* (measures as it captures underemployment.) Tj
ET
BT
