BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 753.8899999999999864 Td
(Industries classified using National Industrial Classification \(NIC\) 2008 \(aligned with ISIC Rev. 4\). Occupations) Tj
T* (classified using National Classification of Occupations \(NCO\) 2015 \(aligned with ISCO-08\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 705.8899999999999864 Td
(4. Key Indicators Produced by PLFS) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 687.8899999999999864 Td
(| Indicator | Definition | Reference Period |) Tj
T* (|---|---|---|) Tj
T* (| LFPR | Labour Force / Population × 100 | UPS, CWS, CDS |) Tj
T* (| WPR | Employed / Population × 100 | UPS, CWS, CDS |) Tj
T* (| Unemployment Rate | Unemployed / LF × 100 | UPS, CWS, CDS |) Tj
T* (| Employment by industry | Distribution across NIC sectors | Usual activity |) Tj
T* (| Employment by occupation | Distribution across NCO categories | Usual activity |) Tj
T* (| Employment by status | Self-employed, regular/salaried, casual | Usual activity |) Tj
T* (| Wages | Wage/earnings by category, sex, sector | Current status |) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 550.8899999999999864 Td
(5. Comparison: PLFS vs. Earlier EUS) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 532.8899999999999864 Td
(| Feature | Earlier NSSO EUS | PLFS |) Tj
T* (|---|---|---|) Tj
T* (| Frequency | Quinquennial \(every 5 years\) | Annual \(rural+urban\) + Quarterly \(urban\) |) Tj
T* (| Design | Cross-sectional | Rotating panel \(urban\) |) Tj
T* (| Sample size | ~1 lakh HHs \(large round\) | ~1 lakh HHs/year \(continuous\) |) Tj
T* (| Urban quarterly data | Not available | Available from PLFS |) Tj
T* (| Reference period | UPS, CWS, CDS | UPS, CWS, CDS \(same\) |) Tj
T* (| Latest base | 2011-12 | 2017-18 \(first full year\) |) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 408.8899999999999864 Td
(6. Practical Example: Computing Unemployment Rate) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 390.8899999999999864 Td
(From a hypothetical PLFS sample for urban areas \(CWS reference period\):) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 369.8899999999999864 Td
(Population \(15+ years\): 1,00,000 persons) Tj
T* (Employed \(CWS\): 42,000) Tj
T* (Unemployed \(seeking + available\): 3,000) Tj
T* (Out of Labour Force \(students, domestic duties, etc.\): 55,000) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 309.8899999999999864 Td
(Labour Force = 42,000 + 3,000 = 45,000) Tj
T* (LFPR = \(45,000 / 1,00,000\) × 100 = 45.0%) Tj
T* (WPR = \(42,000 / 1,00,000\) × 100 = 42.0%) Tj
T* (Unemployment Rate = \(3,000 / 45,000\) × 100 = 6.7%) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 237.8899999999999864 Td
(7. Data Quality Considerations) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 219.8899999999999864 Td
(- **Reporting bias**: Respondents may under-report casual or part-time work, especially women's work in domestic) Tj
T* (enterprises.) Tj
T* (- **Reference period sensitivity**: UPS, CWS, and CDS measures give different results; comparisons across surveys) Tj
T* (must use the same reference period.) Tj
T* (- **Seasonal variation**: Labour market conditions in agriculture vary significantly by season; annual averages may) Tj
T* (mask within-year fluctuations.) Tj
T* (- **Urban-rural comparability**: The rotating panel design is only for urban areas; rural estimates are cross-sectional) Tj
T* (only.) Tj
T* (- **Non-response**: Non-response in follow-up rounds of the panel can introduce attrition bias.) Tj
T* (- **Informal employment**: Self-employed and casual workers are harder to classify; "contributing family workers" are) Tj
T* (counted as employed even with zero earnings.) Tj
