(8. Key Learning Points) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 750.8899999999999864 Td
(1. PLFS replaced the quinquennial NSSO EUS from 2017-18; provides annual \(rural+urban\) and quarterly \(urban\)) Tj
T* (estimates.) Tj
T* (2. The three reference periods \(UPS/UPSS, CWS, CDS\) give different employment and unemployment rates.) Tj
T* (3. Labour force = employed + unemployed \(seeking + available\).) Tj
T* (4. LFPR measures labour market participation; WPR measures employment; UR measures unemployment among the) Tj
T* (labour force.) Tj
T* (5. Urban quarterly estimates use a rotating panel; rural estimates are cross-sectional.) Tj
T* (6. CDS unemployment rate is highest as it captures part-day underemployment.) Tj
ET
